# [GAME_NAME_FULL]

jMonkeyEngine [JME_VERSION], Java [JAVA_VERSION].

`app` contains shared game code and assets. Each `platform-*` module contains only its launcher.

## Prerequisites

Install JDK 21 to run Gradle (this is separate from the selected game Java version).
Foojay automatically downloads the selected compilation/runtime toolchains when absent.
No JDK is bundled with this ZIP.

[IF=DESKTOP]## Desktop

`./gradlew :platform-desktop:run`

Use `:platform-desktop:installDist` or `:platform-desktop:distZip` for a distribution.
Build distributions on their target OS. macOS requires `-XstartOnFirstThread`, already configured.
[/IF=DESKTOP]

[IF=ANDROID]## Android

Install Android SDK platform 36 and Build Tools 36.0.0. Set `ANDROID_HOME` or `sdk.dir`
in an untracked `local.properties`.

`./gradlew :platform-android:assembleDebug`

This template targets API 36 with minSdk [ANDROID_MIN_SDK]. Java 25 is desktop-only.
Keep shared code within Android's available APIs.
[/IF=ANDROID]

[IF=IOS]## iOS

Requires macOS with Xcode, its command-line tools, and an installed iOS Simulator runtime.
libJGLIOS provisions its specialized GraalVM toolchain.

`./gradlew :platform-ios:runIosDebugApp -PiosAppTarget=simulator`

Device builds and signing require your own Apple development team and provisioning configuration.
See [libJGLIOS documentation](https://github.com/NostrGameEngine/libJGLIOS).
[/IF=IOS]

## Community modules

Repositories are centralized in `settings.gradle.kts`; published artifacts, runtime dependencies,
and engine exclusions are in `app/build.gradle.kts`. Original Library snippets are retained under
`gradle/library-snippets/` as non-executable references. GitHub Packages reads
`GITHUB_PACKAGES_USERNAME` and `GITHUB_PACKAGES_TOKEN` from the environment when required.

